er the existing 9f1c8e42 env, the joint enforce/grandfather MECHANISM is proven by a fixture verify-opcert test, and a runbook documents the deferred flip.'","Parent epic AC oracle: 'the deferred-flip runbook exists'","Leaf ACs cover signing round-trip, joint enforce/grandfather posture, and rollback, but make NO mention of a deferred-flip runbook deliverable.","ABSENCE: no sibling ticket is assigned the deferred-flip runbook — the epic assigns it to goose specifically."],"finding":"The leaf omits the deferred-flip RUNBOOK that the parent epic names as an in-scope goose deliverable (and as an explicit AC oracle).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7b91906a646027b3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria; Testing","norm_id":"ncab66bdac06e3379","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The slice closes with signing + mechanism proof but no operator runbook, leaving the deferred flip undocumented and the parent AC 'the deferred-flip runbook exists' unsatisfiable by goose's evidence."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the exact seam by which the rebar-mcp container signs op-certs under the SSM opcert key (e.g. set REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key for the `mcp` compose service, OR have mcp_server.build_server compose+bind an OpcertSigner) — REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY alone is NOT read by ensure_opcert_key, so as wired the container would sign under a self-generated <tracker>/.opcert-key that fails the pinned-env verify.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Provision the rebar-mcp container with the EXISTING nava-opcert-prod signing key (from SSM /rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key) and REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID=9f1c8e42-...' — names REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID (principal) but no key-routing var for the op-cert seam.","src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:180-198 — ensure_opcert_key resolves the op-cert PRIVATE key from: a context-local composed-signer binding, else REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH, else <tracker>/.opcert-key. It never reads REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY.","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:353-356 — the `mcp` service sets REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID and REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key but does NOT set REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH (contrast line 285 where the `opcert` service does).","src/rebar/_opcert_binding.py:1-18 — the composed-signer (compose_signer/bound_signer) path is threaded only by the opcert gate service's run_job; app.py:56 composes it. mcp_server.py has no opcert-key wiring (search for 'opcert' in mcp_server.py: no matches).","Consequence: an unbound MCP process resolves the op-cert key to a self-generated <tracker>/.opcert-key under the correct principal but an UNPINNED key — the AC1 negative/contrast case, not the positive."],"finding":"Move 1 does not name the concrete mechanism (env var / startup signer binding) by which the rebar-mcp CONTAINER routes the op-cert private key into rebar's op-cert signing seam; as currently wired the MCP process would not sign under the pinned key.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5e52337e3e4cddef","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale, move 1; AC1","norm_id":"n40e43c23ea7edb36","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deploy the plan as written; a plan-review/completion cert minted by the rebar-mcp container is verified via trusted_env.verify_required_environment and REJECTED (key_not pinned) because the container signed under a self-generated key, not the SSM opcert key.","AC1's positive assertion ('a cert minted by the container VERIFIES against the pinned pubkey') cannot be satisfied without adding the missing key-routing wiring."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In move 1, specify that the `mcp` service sets REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH to the bind-mounted /run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key (mirroring the opcert service at docker-compose.yml:285), since ensure_opcert_key (src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:189) reads that override and the MCP server does not use the gate service's context-local composed-signer binding.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Realign the leaf to the parent's contract: prove the joint enforce/grandfather MECHANISM via a FIXTURE-CONFIG verify-opcert test rather than committing/performing the flip on the authoritative rebar.toml on main (the parent declares committing the flip OUT OF SCOPE — a deferred operator step).","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1062,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent epic (jira-reb-3527) description: 'Committing the flip (verify.require_environment + verify.opcert_enforce_since) into the authoritative rebar.toml is OUT OF SCOPE for this epic — a deferred operator step, because a local-CLI close signs the completion-verifier cert under the LOCAL env (not 9f1c8e42), so an early flip would fail verify-identity for every local close repo-wide.'","Parent epic AC for goose: 'the joint enforce/grandfather MECHANISM is proven by a fixture-config verify-opcert test, and a runbook documents the deferred flip (spoiled-bionic-goose; committing the flip is OUT OF SCOPE — a deferred operator step)'","Leaf Approach move 2: 'Flip the env-binding gate from advisory to enforcing SAFELY via expand-contract: set verify.opcert_enforce_since to a deploy-time grandfather boundary... AND verify.require_environment to the env_id, together.'","Leaf Compat section: 'touches the authoritative rebar.toml verify posture on main and wires the MCP container to the prod signing key (a human performs/authorizes the key wiring + the flip).'","Leaf AC line 2 asserts require_environment + opcert_enforce_since are 'set together with opcert_enforce_since at a deploy-time boundary' verified 'through the real verify-opcert merged-log walk' — i.e. a real flip, not a fixture-config proof."],"finding":"The leaf makes committing/performing the enforcement flip on the authoritative rebar.toml a central deliverable, but the parent epic explicitly and repeatedly declares committing the flip OUT OF SCOPE for this slice (a deferred operator step).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc3e5365184b0a8bb","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale, move 2; Acceptance Criteria line 2; Compat / rollback / migration-safety","norm_id":"nad224267970b0cb0","priority":0.7438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The leaf's flip lands on main's rebar.toml while local-CLI closes still sign completion-verifier certs under the LOCAL env (not 9f1c8e42), which the parent warns 'would fail verify-identity for every local close repo-wide.'","A reviewer approves the leaf believing the flip is in-scope, defeating the parent's deliberate deferral to an operator step."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Rewrite Approach move 2 and AC line 2 to assert the enforce/grandfather behavior against a FIXTURE rebar.toml (isolated test config), not the authoritative on-main rebar.toml, and drop the 'human performs the flip' from Compat; leave the actual on-main flip to the deferred operator step the parent names. If the author believes the flip truly belongs in this slice, update the parent epic first (re-scoping goose) before diverging the leaf.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"